DEMONSTRATION ONLY (the late frame, docs/measurements/2026-11-20-late-frame.md). Never in a
build that a trial, the gate or a verdict uses; scripts/build-compositor.sh does not know it.

A patch against gst-wayland-display (https://github.com/games-on-whales/gst-wayland-display,
MIT License), commit 1301f86, on top of the four measured patches in scripts/patches, with or
without gst-wayland-display-proposal-draw-before-copy.patch in this folder.

With `ISTESSO_LATE_FRAME_DEMO=N` in the environment the renderer gets extra work before every
frame: N times it fills a buffer of its own that nothing shows. The picture is drawn after that
work. Without the proposal patch the copy into the element's buffer is then asked for while
the renderer is still busy, and takes the picture of the frame before; with the proposal patch
it waits. Without the variable nothing changes.

